      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-116311",
      ":question/problem": "A company manufactures a sports nutritional supplement. The cost and revenue functions, in hundreds of dollars, of this company are given by\n$C(x) = 1000 + 7x, R(x) = 30x - 0.05x^{2}$,\nwhere $x$ represents the number of units produced per month. Find the number of units the company needs to produce in a month to make a profit of $$140000$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
