      ":question/problem": "A company manufactures milk bottles. The cost and revenue functions, in hundreds of dollars, of this company are given by\n$C(x) = 6440 + 48x, R(x) = 240x - 0.8x^{2}$,\nwhere $x$ represents the number of units produced per year. Find the number of units the company needs to produce in a year to make a profit of $$500000$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
